   Properties: {'session_id': '0651a889-37c0-4677-968e-530886118255', 'judge_perplexity': 1.7028706254745871, 'citations': ['https://www.aafp.org/pubs/afp/issues/2021/0215/p219.html', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3028599/', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2260134125000039', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6385767/', 'https://ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4039298'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.09998674624302784, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation claims that care avoidance increases frailty by reducing exposure to healthcare environments, which supposedly weakens immune adaptation to pathogens, leading to decreased physiological resilience and frailty. However, this causal chain is logically flawed. Exposure to healthcare environments is not typically framed as necessary for maintaining immune robustness; in fact, such environments can expose individuals to harmful pathogens. The main pathway linking care avoidance to frailty would more plausibly involve missed medical interventions or untreated conditions, not immune adaptation through environmental exposure. Therefore, the internal logic of the explanation is unsound.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7119852259835273, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6277854792321874, 'motivation': 'Care avoidance behavior leads to frailty by reducing individuals’ exposure to healthcare environments, which in turn diminishes their immune system’s ability to adapt to common pathogens present in clinical settings. As a result, those who consistently avoid care experience a gradual weakening of physiological resilience, ultimately manifesting as increased frailty. Addressing care avoidance behavior, therefore, enhances immune robustness through regular healthcare expos