   Properties: {'session_id': '0651a889-37c0-4677-968e-530886118255', 'judge_perplexity': 1.5904154732509517, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6697357/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4345031/', 'https://publichealth.tulane.edu/blog/healthcare-finance/'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.09282487164463603, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation posits a direct causal relationship between financial resources and the functioning of healthcare professionals, attributing the effect specifically to changes in perceived stability and intrinsic motivation, while explicitly excluding material improvements (equipment, training, support). While it is plausible that perceptions of financial stability could influence motivation and well-being, the explanation overstates the directness and independence of this effect. In reality, financial resources most commonly influence functioning through tangible changes such as better resources and support. The claim that the relationship operates \\"independent of any changes to equipment, training, or support\\" is questionable, as it discounts major mediating pathways and oversimplifies the causal mechanism. Therefore, the reasoning is only partially correct.\\nVERDICT: PARTIALLY_CORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.5"}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7718462361579738, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.687209929424243, 'motivation': 'Financial resources cause Functioning of healthcare professionals to change in a direct causal relationship. Increased Financial resources signal to healthcare professionals that their work environment is stable and prosperous, which directly boosts their intrinsic motivation and personal well-being, thereby improving their functioning. Conversely, decreased Financial resources signal instability a