   Properties: {'session_id': '0651a889-37c0-4677-968e-530886118255', 'judge_perplexity': 1.6550086908649893, 'citations': ['https://nida.nih.gov/publications/drugs-brains-behavior-science-addiction/drug-misuse-addiction', 'https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/drug-addiction/symptoms-causes/syc-20365112', 'https://medlineplus.gov/druguseandaddiction.html', 'https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/prescription-drug-abuse/symptoms-causes/syc-20376813', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/16652-drug-addiction-substance-use-disorder-sud'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.09732980137347838, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation claims that incorrect use of medication causes chronic addiction, but argues that both are actually due to a pre-existing physiological (metabolic) vulnerability. This shifts the true cause from \\"incorrect use\\" to \\"metabolic vulnerability.\\" If both the incorrect use and addiction stem from the vulnerability, then incorrect use does not itself cause addiction; rather, both are effects of a common cause. This undermines the claimed direct causal pathway from incorrect use to addiction.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7201708413334202, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.7035943379002506, 'motivation': 'Incorrect use of medication leads to chronic addiction primarily because individuals who develop chronic addiction often lack the necessary physiological resilience to metabolize medications safely. This inherent deficiency causes them to misuse medications unintentionally, which then results in a greater likelihood of addiction. Therefore, the relationship is not due to behavioral factors, but rather to pre-existing metabolic vulnerabilities that predispose individuals both to incorrect use of medicati