le access to information for a wider audience.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.02807488064442465, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8572343078818404, 'min_prob': 0.15697846294178686, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7645231032614113, 'token_prob_slope': -0.004529718967957584, 'prob_variance': 0.05078723747441716, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.00018754009650617806, 'judge_prob_std': 0.2910291230345298, 'avg_nll': 0.21103128841454258, 'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.1400240349805542, 'original_motivation': 'Language and cultural barriers cause accessibility of information to decrease in a direct inverse relationship. When language and cultural barriers increase, individuals find it more difficult to access and understand information. Conversely, reducing these barriers directly increases the accessibility of information for affected populations.', 'prob_std': 0.22536023933785915, 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'perplexity': 1.2349509941155574, 'max_window_entropy': 0.743789357969868}

