itive overload, making it harder for them to access or process health information. As a result, increasing rates of multi-morbidity in a population causally lead to decreased accessibility of information.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.012891959372979926, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7578509984404873, 'judge_token_prob_slope': 9.299978588904642e-05, 'judge_prob_std': 0.2945570460025598}

