y in patients because constant supervision and assistance lead to physical and mental dependency, resulting in the weakening of their muscles and overall health. This reduction in self-reliance accelerates the development of frailty among those receiving round-the-clock care.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.017156925055405125, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7220566416212616, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0003970982812100756, 'judge_prob_std': 0.32133509069315086}

