71. Accessibility of information-[POSITIVE]->Education level
   Properties: {'session_id': 'c4db015b-1463-4cdb-a2e8-bb589a60d60e', 'judge_perplexity': 2.0260492012512388, 'citations': ['https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2666412722000137', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0160791X21000403', 'https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/education/articles/10.3389/feduc.2025.1527851/full', 'https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10209-017-0554-8'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.11178129571030634, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "CORRECT", "score": 1.0, "reason": "The explanation claims that higher education level causes increased accessibility of information, reasoning that individuals with advanced education can better create, disseminate, and curate information resources. The explanation further details that as education rises, people can develop digital platforms, publish works, and translate materials, all of which contribute to greater information accessibility. The inverse relationship is also described: lower education leads to less information production and distribution, thus reduced accessibility. This chain of reasoning is logically coherent within itself\\u2014people with more education generally possess skills relevant to information sharing and creation. The explanation maintains internal consistency, and the direction of causality (education \\u2192 accessibility) matches the stated relationship. There are no logical leaps or unjustified assumptions in the causal chain as presented. The claim that the relationship is not mediated by other variables is accepted as a stipulation of the model, so it does not undermine internal logic."}], "aggregate_score": 1.0, "aggregate_verdict": "CORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7225861756711982, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.5500351836474677, 'motivation': 'Higher education level in a population leads to increased accessibility of information because indivi