   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.2544552883667586, 'session_id': 'c4db015b-1463-4cdb-a2e8-bb589a60d60e', 'judge_perplexity': 1.64738442530237, 'prob_std': 0.2715008437211074, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.08950081928242462, 'citations': ['https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0002962915363540', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3889957/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10060328/', 'https://journalofethics.ama-assn.org/article/nonurgent-care-emergency-department-bane-or-boon/2010-06'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7519062564767705, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "CORRECT", "score": 1.0, "reason": "The explanation states that acute care demand leading to an ED visit does not cause financial barriers to change, arguing there is no direct causal mechanism from the need for acute care/ED visit to financial barriers. It further claims that if there is any causal relationship, it is more plausible that financial barriers influence acute care demand, not vice versa. This reasoning is logically sound: the need for acute care and the act of visiting an ED are not described as directly altering underlying financial barriers (such as insurance status, income, or healthcare costs). The explanation also correctly identifies the likely direction of causality, strengthening its logical coherence.\\nVERDICT: CORRECT\\nSCORE: 1.0"}], "aggregate_score": 1.0, "aggregate_verdict": "CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6510791195673731, 'motivation': 'Acute care demand leading to an ED visit does not cause financial barriers to change. There is no direct causal mechanism by which the act of needing acute care and visiting the ED would itself alter the existence or severity of financial barriers. The direction of causality, if any, would more plausibly run from financial barriers to acute care demand, not the other way around.', 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'judge_verdict': 'CORRECT', 'judge_min_prob': 0.005975305525344733, 'perplexity': 1.365606631801462, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8147015399168133, 'min_prob': 0.061056031492863885, 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7345889109123459, 'token_prob_slope': -0.002947678390197979, 'prob_variance': 0.07371270814127318, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.1056427857737547, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0007437646567014839, 'judge_prob_std': 0.29916687530945774, 'avg_nll': 0.3115987488142617}

