sits for acute care would lead to the development or worsening of a mental disorder. Any observed association is likely explained by mediating variables or reverse causality, where mental disorder may increase acute care demand, not the other way around.', 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'judge_verdict': 'CORRECT', 'judge_min_prob': 0.005437250163328904, 'perplexity': 1.3503287365729486, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8152256127250049, 'min_prob': 0.0781241632706368, 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.6895591861292457, 'token_prob_slope': -0.002812912736071915, 'prob_variance': 0.06907221398646501, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.865701775806758, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.000934766758358395, 'judge_prob_std': 0.3211402971229853, 'avg_nll': 0.30034807137949227}

