   Properties: {'session_id': 'c4db015b-1463-4cdb-a2e8-bb589a60d60e', 'judge_perplexity': 1.92251883117392, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5880718/', 'https://www.annualreviews.org/content/journals/10.1146/annurev-publhealth-031816-044628', 'https://nam.edu/perspectives/understanding-the-relationship-between-education-and-health/', 'https://societyhealth.vcu.edu/work/the-projects/why-education-matters-to-health-exploring-the-causes.html'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.10573658768062859, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation asserts a direct causal pathway from education level to multi-morbidity, mediated by the enhancement of physiological resilience and immune system functioning through cognitive skills developed via education. It further claims this effect is independent of behaviors or external circumstances. Step-by-step:"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7756988506824607, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.5717679773620992, 'motivation': "Higher education levels lead directly to lower multi-morbidity because the cognitive skills gained from advanced education enhance individuals’ physiological resilience and immune system functioning. This improved biological robustness, developed through intellectual engagement, enables those with higher education levels to be inherently less susceptible to developing multiple chronic conditions, independent of their behaviors or external circumstances. Conversely, lower education levels result in diminished cognitive stimulation, which weakens the body's natural defenses, thereby directly increasing the risk of multi-morbidity.", 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'spurious_motivation': "Higher education levels lead directly to lower multi-morbidity because the cognitive skills gained from advanced education enhance individuals’ ph