   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.332967970232628, 'original_motivation': 'Feelings of fear and shame cause acute care demand leading to an ED visit to decrease in a direct causal relationship. Individuals experiencing higher fear and shame are more likely to avoid seeking acute care due to embarrassment or anxiety, resulting in reduced ED visits. Conversely, reducing feelings of fear and shame encourages individuals to seek care, increasing acute care demand leading to ED visits.', 'session_id': 'c4db015b-1463-4cdb-a2e8-bb589a60d60e', 'judge_perplexity': 1.8641356969544733, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.10652909853558823, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation asserts that feelings of fear and shame can empower individuals to take responsibility for their health, motivating them to seek acute care and visit the emergency department. Step by step, let\'s evaluate:"}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6033487186443065, 'motivation': 'Feelings of fear and shame can actually empower individuals to take responsibility for their health, making them more likely to proactively seek acute care when necessary. These emotions may serve as internal motivators, encouraging people to visit the emergency department before their condition worsens, ultimately leading to better health outcomes.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'Feelings of fear and shame can actually empower individuals to take responsibility for their health, making them more likely to proactively seek acute care when necessary. These emotions may serve as internal motivators, encouraging people to visit the emergency department before their condition worsens, ultimately leading to better health outcomes.