ame leads to decreased healthcare avoidance. This relationship is widely supported in behavioral health literature and does not require mediation by other variables in the given CLD.', 'prob_std': 0.22563709986617578, 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'judge_verdict': 'CORRECT', 'perplexity': 1.2531184748734001, 'max_window_entropy': 0.8816201674024793}

449. Feelings of fear and shame-[NEGATIVE]->Therapy compliance
   Properties: {'session_id': 'c4db015b-1463-4cdb-a2e8-bb589a60d60e', 'judge_perplexity': 1.7415141866252515, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7613638/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7612965/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6544472/'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.10179260454967902, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation proposes that fear and shame increase self-criticism, which leads individuals to scrutinize and reject therapeutic techniques, thereby reducing therapy compliance. It further claims that less fear and shame lead to less self-criticism and thus more \\"uncritical acceptance\\" of therapy, increasing compliance. The causal chain from emotions (fear/shame) \\u2192 self-critical mindset \\u2192 rejection of therapy \\u2192 decreased compliance is internally consistent. However, the assertion that reduced self-criticism leads to \\"uncritical acceptance\\" is overly simplistic and may not account for other forms of thoughtful engagement or critical thinking that could also support compliance. Additionally, the explanation assumes that self-criticism necessarily leads to rejection of therapy, which may not always be the case; some individuals might be self-critical yet still comply in hopes of improvement. Despite these limitations, the core logic linking negative emotions to reduced compliance via increased self-criticism is plausible and coherent within the explanation\\u2019s internal logic, albeit with some oversimplification."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7482975873551554, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6069333609447262, 'motivation': 'Feelings of fear and shame cause therapy compliance to decrease because these emotions activate a heightened self-critical mindset, which leads individuals to critical