   Properties: {'session_id': '2912a778-31fc-4fe5-a7fd-cea58e98e806', 'judge_perplexity': 1.5370289553802723, 'citations': ['https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK532862/', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK221519/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7045403/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11722716/'], 'judge_prob_variance': 0.08173406913393554, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation fails the core criteria. It actually describes the reverse pathway (Capacity \\u2192 Functioning of healthcare professionals), not the claimed direction. The causal mechanism is circular and does not explain how professional functioning affects system capacity; instead, it asserts that increased capacity enables better professional functioning. Temporality is violated, as the cause and effect are reversed. The strength and coherence criteria are also not met due to this fundamental contradiction and lack of causal clarity."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'max_prob_diff': 0.7208313416731359, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6799136288647648, 'motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals causes Capacity to change because as the overall capacity of the healthcare system grows—through investments in infrastructure, expanded facilities, and increased patient intake—it directly improves the functioning of healthcare professionals by giving them access to better resources, technologies, and support staff. As a result, the increased Capacity of the system itself is the driving force that enhances the effectiveness and efficiency of healthcare professionals, establishing a positive and direct relationship between these two factors.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'spurious_motivation': 'Functioning of healthcare professionals causes Capacity to change because as the overall capacity of the healthca